kosha trajectory

  -- trajectory: a path through akasham parameterized by kaala
  -- the root is gati — gati's own shabda is "direction-as-trajectory"
  -- trajectory is gati made precise: a function from kaala to position in sthira-apeksha
  -- in a kinematic chain: trajectory is kona(t) from theta-start to theta-target

  "gati-swarupa krama-sthita kaala-yukta"
  "sthira-apeksha-sthita chala-apeksha-krama-phala"
  "akasham-sthita bindu-krama-siddha"
  "angular-displacement-janaka path-energy-janaka"
  "kinematics-varga-vishesa"

